        "author": "Fabien Dany (Fabienkhan)",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-2.5",
        "observed": "Actually viewed southern court façade:two short square open pavilion heads with gold finials above tall central pointed blind iwan,side recessed fields,blue inscription band,rose-toned mosaic fields,stone base,pointed side galleries and rectangular raised-edge pool. Original broad geometric bands stand in for floral tilework;no picture pixels,calligraphy or copied art used."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nasr_ol_Molk_mosque2.jpg",
        "date": "2008-10-03 (metadata;description says April2008)",
        "author": "dynamosquito",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-2.0",
        "observed": "Actually viewed south façade and both long courtyard ranges:pointed gallery openings with recessed timber/lattice doors or shadowed backs,tall central blind iwan with patterned stepped vault and three pointed bottom fields,low flat parapets,twin open square pavilions and long rectangular pool. This is a court view,not evidence of the unseen outside walls or winter prayer-hall interior."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Iran_2007_097_Nasir-ol-molk_mosque_Shiraz.jpg",
        "date": "2007-10-10",
        "author": "DAVID HOLT",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-2.0",
        "observed": "Actually viewed a north-side minor niche:deep pointed arch,stepped muqarnas-like cells,pink/yellow/blue floral tile fields and closed lower backing with a shallow pointed doorway. Selected stepped vault pieces and broad pink/blue bands abstract this relief;the picture does not establish the entire opposite façade."
      }
